5. Rani Ma'am's important "DIE" examples

This is one of the most useful parts of Rule 60.

The notes give different prepositions after die, depending on the cause/circumstance.

① Die OF — Disease

He died of malaria. ✅

Use of for a disease/illness.

die of cancer
die of malaria

② Die IN — Accident

He died in an accident. ✅

Here the accident is the circumstance/event in which the death occurred.

die in an accident

③ Die FROM — Injury / external cause

He died from a wound. ✅

FROM is used when the death results from an injury or other external cause.

④ Die OF — Hunger / starvation / thirst

He died of hunger. ✅

He died of thirst. ✅

Here hunger/thirst is treated as the cause.

⑤ Die WITH — Grief / sorrow / shame

He died with grief. ✅

The notes associate with with emotions/conditions such as:

grief
sorrow
shame
⑥ Die BY — Violence

He died by violence. ✅

Here by indicates the means/manner of death.
